From 6d8a8bdfa652498c45734d482e3bb188f41fbc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:35:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v1.6.7: Reaper Diagnostics - one-click sanitized diag report
 (Administration tab)

New Administration > Diagnostics tab (Reaper_Diag.asp, reaper-native) with a
single Download action. The baked collector /usr/sbin/reaper_diag (busybox
ash, model-agnostic: radios/ports discovered at runtime) gathers identity,
radio/port/accel/QoS state, lease counts, services and log tails, then pushes
the WHOLE report through one redaction pass: secret nvram values scrubbed
longest-first (presence shown as SET/EMPTY), MACs -> MAC-n pseudonyms
(consistent within a report), SSIDs/usernames/hostnames -> tokens, all IPv6
and public IPv4 -> tokens (RFC1918/loopback/multicast and firmver kept). A
sanitization ledger heads every report.

- others/reaper_diag + Makefile install (0700, /usr/sbin)
- httpd do_reaper_diag_cgi (do_auth, text/plain): runs collector, accepts
  only /tmp/reaper_diag_* paths, lockfile vs overlapping runs, streams then
  unlinks; body starts with ERROR: on failure (page JS surfaces it)
- Reaper_Diag.asp: collected/masked/how-it-works cards, ledger sample,
  download row with do-not-navigate warning, busy overlay (Collecting data
  with building dots), XHR blob download named reaper_diag_<model>_<ts>.txt
- menuTrees/menuTree.js: Administration tab entry (shell tab strip picks it
  up; topbar/rail untouched)
- RDIAG_00..31 appended to all 25 dicts in lockstep (translated)
